WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.560
Chad, I understand you moved to Los Angeles
in 1995?

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:03.560
1996.

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:09.050
Do you think you worker hard now than you
did in 1996?

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:12.400
Or is it the same but a different type of
working at it?

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.589
It’s a different type of working at it.

00:00:14.589 --> 00:00:21.640
Like I said, when I first moved here I had
blinders on and you don’t realize what you’re

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.670
getting into, what this means.

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:30.199
And so I worked very hard to break into the
business and I got lucky that it happened

00:00:30.199 --> 00:00:33.900
at a very early age.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:39.620
You have to work just as hard, if not harder,
once you do get some success.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:46.350
I think you have to keep working to hopefully
keep that success although this business is

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:50.280
up and down and it doesn’t seem to be anywhere
in between.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:55.730
At least for me it seems like you have those
good years and then you have years where you

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:56.930
don’t work.

00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:58.380
You have to ride it out.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:02.710
A lot of actors will ask “What do you suggest?

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:03.710
What’s your advice?”

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:07.790
And what I say is “Persistence is key.

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:09.110
Don’t leave.”

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:16.460
“Be the last one standing” is what my
acting coach said to me.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:18.260
Be the last one standing.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:19.960
So you have to.

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:24.270
Don’t give up because if you give up that
might have been the next day where you got

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.680
that audition that is going to change your
life.

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:30.900
So if it’s who you are, don’t give up.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:32.659
You can’t.

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:38.230
As much as you might want to….as much as
I have days where I’m like “Aaaargh!”

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:44.510
I just want to say “Peace Out” and run
and go the other way but then I would be miserable

00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:46.740
because it is who I am.

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:53.550
I know we talked about this a long time ago
in 2012 where you said you knew that this

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:54.990
was the choice you were going to make.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:02:00.280
Maybe you can revisit this for us where…do
you remember the exact moment where you said

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:01.280
to yourself This Is What I Want!

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:02.590
Where you weren’t going to be o.k.

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:06.590
if you said to yourself “You know what,
why don’t I get a job” or go back to a

00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:09.619
vocational school and try to get a desk job
or something?

00:02:09.619 --> 00:02:12.310
When did you know that this was for you?

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:20.370
I knew….I knew in high school that is what
I wanted to do at a very early age.

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:22.200
Nobody was going to tell me differently.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:30.990
You know, looking back I don’t think I’m…I’m
not the guy to sit behind a desk at an office.

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:32.690
Not that there is anything wrong with that.

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.730
It’s just not who I am.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:42.920
I’m kind of used to the uncertainty now
and sort of crazy off life it is to be an

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:43.920
actor.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.560
It’s not a regular thing.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:47.740
There is no certainty in this business.

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:50.390
There is mostly uncertainty.

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:53.780
So you kind of have to roll with that.

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:56.990
Interesting….so being comfortable with being
uncomfortable?

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:57.990
Exactly.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:58.990
Yes.

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:02.170
It’s being comfortable with being uncomfortable
which is pretty much all the time.

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:06.120
And then you’ll have a couple great months
where you work and you go on location.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:11.730
The last movie I did, I went to Bulgaria for
a month and a half and got to work with Antonio

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:15.330
Banderas and Sir Ben Kingsley.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:18.060
It was amazing.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:21.070
And then you return and it’s back to reality.

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:26.540
So…[laughs] it’s a very weird business.

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:29.360
It changes on a dime and that is what I love
about it!

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:30.800
You just never know.

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:31.800
You just never know.

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:32.800
Question for the viewers.

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:33.203
Tell us about the moment you decided to pursue
an entertainment career.

